{
  "id": "ss.lib.arm",
  "name": "Survivor arm",
  "description": "One arm of the survivor caste, hinged at the shoulder: origin at the joint, limb hanging down +y, so a `rot` track swings it from where an arm actually swings. A tapered shaft, an elbow plate, and a forked tarsal claw for a hand — two prongs, the way the hive grips, which is the one place these bodies most obviously stopped being hive and never quite became anything else. Same cold slate as `ss.lib.leg`; whatever colour a survivor wears is plate over this, never this. `far` is the arm behind the body, a step darker and without its ink line.",
